You can use the Google Maps API to get the user's current location. Here are the steps:
1. Sign up for a Google account and create an application.
2. Install the Google Maps JavaScript API in your web browser.
3. Create a new page with the following code:
```
<script src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY&callback=initMap" async defer></script>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
function initMap() {
  var map = new google.maps.Map(document.getElementById('map'), {
    center: {lat: -34.397, lng: 150.644},
    zoom: 8
  });
}
</script>
```
Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual API key from the Google Cloud Console.
4. Add a marker to the map that shows the user's current location.
5. Use the `getCurrentPosition()` method of the `google.maps.Marker` object to get the user's current position as a JSON object.
Here is some sample code to get you started:
```
var currentPosition = {};
function getCurrentPosition(position) {
  currentPosition.lat = position.coords.latitude;
  currentPosition.lng = position.coords.longitude;
  return currentPosition;
}
var currentPosition = getCurrentPosition();
console.log(currentPosition);
```
This will log the user's current position as a JSON object to the console. You can then use this information to send a message or perform other actions based on the user's location.

